# RSF04-01: what a cache may keep.
title Every request inside the definition may be kept by a cache; a made-up path or parameter is answered too, but never kept
row  req:box "GET /news/?page=2" | def:warnbox "Inside the definition?" "cache-path, cache-query" | keep:okbox "May be kept" "by any cache"
row  odd:box "GET /news/?x=8f3a" "made up" | nokeep:nobox "Answered, not kept" "Cache-Control: no-store"
arrow req -> def
arrow def -> keep "yes" go
arrow odd -> def
arrow def -> nokeep "no"
note Nothing is refused: the definition may lag behind the site, a page published a second ago still works.
